CLUB: Frankford Radio Club
SOAPBOX: Got inspired to try FT8/FT4 at the Cumberland Amateur Radio Club Field Day,
SOAPBOX: enough to install and use WSJT-X standalone. PTCP inspired me to try FT8
SOAPBOX: contesting. After taking time to integrate WSJT-X, N1MM+ and Enterlogic VSPE for
SOAPBOX: my IC7300, 99w, 4-band vertical, it worked! Amazed to QSO VU22DX, and there were
SOAPBOX: always stations available. Had several nice runs even. The contesting pace is
SOAPBOX: slower & less frantic than other modes, even RTTY, allowing more BIC hours.
SOAPBOX: I'm all-in on FT8, but in my shack NOTHING tops CW!
CREATED-BY: WW-DIGI Adif Converter
